    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Run the whole suite with `make test` (the Makefile target sets PYTHONPATH=src for the src layout); there is no `tools/test` script, and bare `python -m unittest` fails to import tally.",
    "helpful": 7,
    "harmful": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "tests/test_ledger.py reads .fixtures/golden.json, which is gitignored and not in the repo: generate it first with `./tools/gen-fixtures --seed 4c1579150fca` (the team seed) before running the suite; it prints `fixtures written to .fixtures/golden.json`.",
    "helpful": 8,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "For cut a tally release (version bump, changelog fold of Unreleased, checksum, single commit, annotated tag): load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "Run the CLI by hand as `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m tally <cmd>` from the repo root; `cd src` first breaks it, since DEFAULT_LEDGER is the relative path `data/sample.ledger`.",
    "helpful": 3,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "Validate CLI arguments with an argparse `type=` function that raises `argparse.ArgumentTypeError` (like `_date`); malformed values then exit 2 — but argparse raises `SystemExit(2)` instead of returning, so the `run` helper in tests/test_cli.py catches `SystemExit` and uses `e.code`.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "For add a new `tally <subcommand>` (parser, report function, exit code, tests, docs): load the `tally-new-command` skill first and follow its steps.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p7",
    "text": "Every change gets a bullet under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md, added in the same pass as the code change (style: `- ` bullets with backticked identifiers like `money.split`); leaving it out is a review failure.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p8",
    "text": "This sandbox has no outbound network: a real `tally sync` run fails with `<urlopen error [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution>` before reaching the server, so never judge a network command by a hand run — prove it with `urllib.request.urlopen` mocked in the test.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p9",
    "text": "Hand-testing against staging uses `TALLY_URL=https://staging.tally.example`; the matching `$TALLY_TOKEN` is supplied by the user in the request and never written into the repo, tests or docs (README shows `TALLY_TOKEN=...`).",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]
